"The reviewed setup package is ready for **Tidewater Kayak Hire**: five milestones and 16 tickets, plus Storybloq’s default setup phase.\n\nThe first version covers 1/2/4-hour bookings, payment at the kiosk, free cancellation at least 48 hours before departure, staff checkout/return tracking, and weather cancellations with customer texts. Online payment and guided tours remain deferred.\n\nUsing your delegated judgement, I propose **Python/Django, PostgreSQL, and server-rendered pages**. The SMS provider and hosting remain implementation choices.\n\n| Milestone and demonstration | Ticket | Purpose | Depends on |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Foundation: configured service and reviewed prototype | P01 | Establish application and verification tooling | — |\n| | P02 | Configure staff access, fleet, prices and trading hours | P01 |\n| | P03 | Prototype customer and staff journeys | — |\n| | P04 | **Checkpoint:** owner reviews prototype | P03 |\n| Reservations: customers can book and cancel | P05 | Calculate available slots without overbooking | P02 |\n| | P06 | Save bookings securely and handle duplicate submissions | P05 |\n| | P07 | Build booking and confirmation screens | P06, P04 |\n| | P08 | Provide secure cancellation with the 48-hour cutoff | P06, P04 |\n| Operations: staff can run the hire day | P09 | Show daily bookings and record out/returned kayaks | P06, P02, P04 |\n| | P10 | **Checkpoint:** demonstrate booking and hire operations | P07–P09 |\n| Weather: close a day and track customer texts | P11 | Cancel active reservations safely, preserving equipment tracking | P06, P02 |\n| | P12 | Send weather texts with retries and visible failures | P11 |\n| | P13 | Build staff closure confirmation and delivery-status screens | P11, P12, P04 |\n| Release: demonstrate a verified, operable service | P14 | Verify complete journeys, permissions and failure recovery | P07–P09, P13 |\n| | P15 | Prepare deployment, backups, staff runbook and real SMS check | P14 |\n| | P16 | **Checkpoint:** owner accepts the first version | P10, P15 |\n\nThese are provisional ticket labels; Storybloq will assign IDs during creation. **P01 and P03 can begin independently.** Checkpoints are ordinary tickets; Storybloq does not technically enforce owner approval.\n\nThe main labelled assumptions are:\n\n- One kayak per reservation; customers use a secure management link without creating an account.\n- Cancellation inside 48 hours directs customers to staff; no fee is invented.\n- Weather closure includes customers currently out and preserves return tracking. Completed and previously cancelled bookings are excluded.\n- Actual fleet, hours, prices, business timezone, support contact and data-retention settings are established before launch.\n\nIndependent review identified the active-hire weather-notification gap; that correction is incorporated. No other material findings remain, and the dependency graph has no cycles.\n\nApproval covers creating `.story/`, the roadmap and tickets, an initial snapshot, handover and setup note, plus:\n\n| File | Content |\n|---|---|\n| `AGENTS.md` | Product scope, proposed architecture, assumptions and source decisions |\n| `RULES.md` | Booking/cancellation rules, privacy, permissions and tests-first development for business logic |\n| `REVIEW.md` | The skill’s standard review contract |\n| `.gitignore` | Storybloq runtime files, local environment files and Python caches |\n\nIt also covers initializing Git. No commit, push, paid provisioning or application implementation is included.\n\nI propose **Full pipeline** because booking and cancellation involve business rules and concurrent updates. All stages initially stay **disabled**, since this folder has no established tooling:\n\n| Stage | Proposed command, pending P01 |\n|---|---|\n| WRITE_TESTS / TEST | `python manage.py test` |\n| BUILD | `python manage.py collectstatic --noinput` |\n| VERIFY | `python manage.py runserver 127.0.0.1:8000`, checked at `/health/` |\n\nWould you like to **approve setup**, adjust the plan, or inspect ticket/file details?\n\nThe story [setup instructions](/private/tmp/cc-cpm-w4-t525/onboarding-eval-ImgJTp/home/.agents/skills/story/setup-flow.md) require “One approval of the setup package” before creation. The review is complete; nothing has been written yet."
